1
00:00:00,780 --> 00:00:08,364
Good morning, explorers! Today we're following one tiny raindrop on an amazing journey through the water cycle.

2
00:00:09,744 --> 00:00:16,728
When sunshine warms oceans, lakes, and puddles, where does the water go? Watch closely.

3
00:00:18,294 --> 00:00:26,814
It becomes invisible water vapor and rises. This is evaporation—the sun gives water energy to climb into the sky.

4
00:00:28,844 --> 00:00:36,836
High above us, cooler air turns vapor into tiny droplets. They gather into clouds. This is condensation.

5
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:48,226
When clouds become heavy, water falls as rain, snow, or hail. This is precipitation, returning water to Earth.

6
00:00:50,894 --> 00:00:53,030
Can anyone complete the cycle?

7
00:00:53,450 --> 00:01:03,242
Evaporation, condensation, precipitation—and collection, as rivers, soil, and oceans gather the water.

8
00:01:03,662 --> 00:01:09,998
Exactly! Water keeps traveling around and around. Every drop has a story.
